        "original_id": "4bd8c2c0-788e-53ee-952a-ce1d32e8e650",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Ghosts (2006 film)\n- Concepts: Gweilo, Cantonese slang\n- Topics: Ethnicity, racial language\n\nFacts:\n- Ghosts (2006 film) takes its title from the Cantonese slang term \"Gweilo\" (鬼佬), which means \"ghost man.\"\n- Gweilo in its unmodified form is used for white people and applies only to people of European ethnicities.\n- Gweilo has a history of racially deprecatory use.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
